-- title:
--   Rational crossing points are closed with residue field O/𝔪
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. a Deligne–Rapoport-style model $X(N_0,q)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{DRLevel.R } q)$ packaged together with its properness, flatness, integrality, normality on affine opens, generic smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality, its identification with a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the modular function field of level $N_0q$ compatibly with the Galois action and the Igusa charts, and the distinguished sections. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O \colon \mathtt{DRLevel.R } q \to O$ and maximal ideal generated by $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$, and let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathtt{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\,0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathtt{comp}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\,1$ (the two branches over $\kappa$). Write $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathtt{crossingPt}\,\rho_O\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\,n$ for the image of $n$ in $\mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\,\rho_O$ under the first projection followed by the zeroth branch morphism followed by $\mathtt{DRLevel.bcMap}\,\rho_O\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Assume the generic points $\mathfrak X.\xi_{\inf}$ and $\mathfrak X.\xi_{\mathrm{zero}}$ both specialise to $x_n$, and assume $x_n$ is rational over the residue field of $O$: there is a morphism $s \colon \operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m) \to \mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\,\rho_O$ whose composite with the second projection of the relevant pullback square equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $O \to O/\mathfrak m$, and which sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m)$ to $x_n$. The conclusion is twofold: the map sending $o \in O$ to the residue class in the residue field of the local ring $\mathcal O_{X_O,x_n}$ of the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $\mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\,\rho_O$ obtained from $o$ via the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ is surjective, and the singleton $\{x_n\}$ is closed in $\mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\,\rho_O$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a point of a scheme over a local ring $O$ which is cut out by a section over the residue field $O/\mathfrak m$ is a closed point whose residue field is generated by the image of $O$; here it is applied to the crossing point of the two branches of the special fibre of the level-$(N_0,q)$ Deligne–Rapoport model after base change to $O$. It feeds the construction of oriented crossing charts at such a point, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
